<title>SINGAPORE: Van Der Horst half yr profit down 84 pct.</title>
<headline>Van Der Horst half yr profit down 84 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			   4.14    vs     25.40</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		  3.8     vs     23.7</p>
<p>    Turnover			    27.56    vs     74.12</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest    1.93    vs	4.13</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		 5.39    vs	1.36</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)	   2.59    vs	2.18</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	  7.06    vs	0.07 (loss)</p>
<p>    Pre-tax (loss)		     2.07    vs     26.63 (profit)</p>
<p>    Tax				    0.85    vs	1.17</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		    nil     vs	0.29 (loss)</p>
<p>Note - Van der Horst Ltd is an infrastructure engineering company with substantial business interest in Indonesia.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
